        "message": {
          "content": "A) Stay in the city\n\nLeaving achieves nothing to relieve the child's suffering; it merely subtracts your own well-being and the positive contributions you could make to the lives of your family and community. While the child's misery is a profound tragedy, walking away is a purely symbolic gesture that produces a net loss of happiness in the world without sparing anyone any pain. Given that the child's torment cannot be undone by your departure, the most rational course is to remain where the greatest amount of joy, flourishing, and peace can still be realized.",
